            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"week-12-recency-in-practice\">Week 12: recency in practice</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Deliverable:</strong> refresh one source, rerun your checks, report what changed.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Public data is not a fixed thing. CMS refreshes Care Compare on a schedule (the course data mirror's\nREADME says quarterly), and every refresh can add or drop hospitals, change numbers, move the\nreporting period forward, or suppress a value that used to be published. An app built in week 8 can\nbe out of date by week 14 without anyone touching it.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This notebook compares two versions of the layer:</span>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Earlier:</strong> your week-3 export (upload it), or a <strong>SIMULATED</strong> earlier snapshot the notebook makes\n  for you, so you can practise before any real refresh.</li>\n<li><strong>Current:</strong> the layer rebuilt now from the sources the course loads today.</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The real exercise is to run this again <strong>after the next refresh</strong> with your saved export, and\nreport what actually changed.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
