          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"5-what-it-means-for-your-app\">5. What it means for your app</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A diff is a list; your report says what it <strong>means</strong>. For each kind of change, decide:</span>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Period moved forward:</strong> your app's labels and your week-5 defense name a period. Are they now wrong?</li>\n<li><strong>Score changed:</strong> is the change bigger than you'd expect from one more quarter of data? Check one\n  hospital against the source page before you believe it.</li>\n<li><strong>New suppression:</strong> a hospital that disappears from your chart has not improved or closed; it lost\n  its number. Does your app say so?</li>\n<li><strong>Rows added or removed:</strong> did your row counts in the app's panel change? They should.</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Ask your AI:</strong> <em>\"Here is the summary of changes between two versions of my data layer: [paste the\nsummary line and the tables]. Draft a half-page 'what changed' note for a hospital manager. List\nevery number you use and which table it came from, so I can check each one.\"</em></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Ask your AI:</strong> <em>\"My week-3 layer has these extra columns: [paste]. Add them to the <code>checks</code>\nfunction in this marimo cell [paste the cell's code], one check per column, and keep the earlier and\ncurrent columns side by side.\"</em></span>\n</blockquote></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ZHCJ",
      "code_hash": "563622510b0c16287241ec68541cb65f",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"before-you-submit\">Before you submit</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Deliverable:</strong> a short \"what changed\" report: which source you refreshed (with its provenance row),\nthe before-and-after checks table, and what the changes mean for your app. If you used the simulated\nsnapshot, say so, and say when you will rerun it on a real refresh.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>The one check:</strong> pick one hospital from \"Hospitals whose score changed\" (or \"New suppression\") and\nconfirm the current value on the source page yourself.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Human sign-off</strong> (three lines in the cell below). AI can help you draft this; make sure every claim is one you can explain live, without the AI open.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
